{%- comment -%}
  The newsletter signup, once.

  This form existed twice, byte for byte: in the footer band (on every page) and
  in sections/newsletter.liquid (a band a merchant can drop into a page). The
  success message is a promise about a discount code, so the two copies drifting
  apart is the expensive kind of duplication -- one of them would have gone on
  offering a code the other had stopped mentioning.

  WELCOME10 is named here and in the footer's Newsletter subtext setting. If the
  code is ever renamed or withdrawn, both say so, and so does the discount in
  Shopify admin. The exclusion is not decoration: the code is scoped to a
  collection of everything NOT tagged pharmacist-review, so medicines are never
  discounted, and saying so before someone adds one to their bag is the whole
  point of the sentence.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% form 'customer', style: 'display:flex; gap:0;' %}
  {% if form.posted_successfully? %}
    <p style="margin:0; padding:10px 14px; color:var(--c-success); font-weight:700; font-size:13.5px;">Welcome! Use code WELCOME10 for 10% off your first order. Excludes medicines.</p>
  {% else %}
    <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter">
    <input type="email" name="contact[email]" required aria-label="Email address" autocomplete="email" placeholder="Enter your email address" style="flex:1; min-width:0; border:none; outline:none; padding:10px 14px; font-family:inherit; font-size:13.5px; color:#2A2B2A; background:transparent;">
    <button type="submit" class="btn-sm btn-fill" style="flex:0 0 auto">Subscribe</button>
  {% endif %}
{% endform %}
